<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75052" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρθρος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the time just before</i> or
				<i>about daybreak, dawn, cock-crow</i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ᾽ ὄρθρου μέχρι περ ἂν ἥλιος
					ἀνάσχῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					951d
				</span></i>
			), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάχα δ᾽ ὄ. ἐγίγνετο δημιοεργός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					98
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπειδὰν ὄ. ᾖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					256
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Av.</u>
				496
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρθρου</span>”
				<i>at dawn,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					577
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Sopat.
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristopho
				10
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρθρου γενομένου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.198
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμα ὄρθρῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.188
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.112
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς ὄρθρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					18.56
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				6.6
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ὄρθρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					772
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ ὄρθρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.101
				</span></i>
			 (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίορθρος</span>) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ὄρθρον</span> towards <i>dawn,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				1089
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ὄρθρον γ᾽ ἐστίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπ᾽ ὄρθρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Batr.
					103
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τὸν ὄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					76.17
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ὄ.,</span> abs., <i>in the
				morning,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.181
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ὄρθρων</span> each
				<i>morning early,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				909
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄ. βαθύς</span> dim
				<i>morning twilight,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλὰ νῦν ὄ. β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					216
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cri.</u>
				43a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				18.14
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς παρελθούσης νυκτὸς . . , ἔτι
					βαθέος ὄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					310a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				24.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄρθρος</span></b> , ὁ, a mythical dog, son of Typhaon and Echidna, that kept
			the herds of Geryoneus on the island Erytheia, and was there killed
			by Heracles, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				309
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				293
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄρθος</span>
			).</div>
